content.text:
Use the `@utility` directive instead of `@layer components` — only utilities registered with `@utility` work with variants like `md:`.

```css
/* globals.css */
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```

```html
<h3 className="md:test">text</h3>
```

Source: `src/docs/functions-and-directives.mdx` (`@utility` section) — "Use the `@utility` directive to add custom utilities to your project that work with variants like `hover`, `focus` and `lg`." Plain classes in `@layer components` (as in `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`) don't get variant support.

